    <h2>What We Publish</h2>
    <p>We publish practical Japanese articles about overseas SaaS tools, AI workflows, website building, newsletters, CRM, ecommerce, analytics, and affiliate program research. The site is built as an ongoing solo-business lab, so application logs, rejected applications, profile improvements, and decision records are also documented.</p>
    <p>Our goal is not to push generic deals or coupon traffic. We focus on helping Japanese readers understand whether a tool fits a small operation before they sign up.</p>

    <h2>Positioning</h2>
    <p>Hitori Jigyo Lab is best understood as a niche Japanese publisher for early-stage solo operators. It does not present itself as a large media company or a coupon marketplace. The strength of the site is specific context: how a Japan-based individual operator checks overseas tools before using them in a real small business.</p>
    <p>Partner teams can review the site as an editorial partner focused on education, tool selection, and low-risk first trials. Traffic is still being developed, but the content base, disclosure structure, and comparison pages are being built deliberately.</p>

    <h2>Primary Reader Intent</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Choosing a website, newsletter, CRM, analytics, or ecommerce tool</li>
      <li>Understanding pricing, free plans, cancellation flow, and Japanese-language usability</li>
      <li>Learning how overseas SaaS can be used in a small Japanese business</li>
      <li>Comparing tools before making a low-risk first trial</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Promotion Methods</h2>
    <p>Hitori Jigyo Lab promotes partner products through editorial articles, comparison pages, tool hubs, application logs, and context-specific links. We do not position the site as a coupon directory, cashback community, trademark-bidding operation, or mass social posting account.</p>
    <p>Affiliate links are disclosed clearly. We prefer practical, trust-first content that explains who a tool is for, who should avoid it, what to check before payment, and what alternatives may exist. The site also operates an X account, <a href="https://x.com/hitorijigyolab">@hitorijigyolab</a>, for short updates and ongoing experiment logs.</p>

    <h2>What We Do Not Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No coupon scraping, cashback positioning, or deal-only pages</li>
      <li>No brand keyword bidding, impersonation, or misleading official-looking pages</li>
      <li>No spam posting, automated comment promotion, or forced sign-up tactics</li>
      <li>No claims about pricing, features, or commissions without checking official information</li>
      <li>No recommendation based only on commission rate</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="review-score-grid">
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">Content</p>
        <h2>Review Articles</h2>
        <p>Long-form Japanese reviews and setup notes written for small operators.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
