    <h2>Current Focus Areas</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Overseas SaaS tools for Japanese solo founders</li>
      <li>AI-assisted workflows and site building</li>
      <li>Newsletter and audience-building tools</li>
      <li>CRM and customer-management tools for small operators</li>
      <li>Image production workflows for affiliate articles</li>
      <li>Analytics and Search Console preparation</li>
      <li>Affiliate network application readiness</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reader Journey</h2>
    <div class="journey-grid">
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">1. Problem</p>
        <h2>Reader has a practical task</h2>
        <p>Build a site, start a newsletter, manage leads, create article images, or understand analytics.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">2. Research</p>
        <h2>Article or comparison page</h2>
        <p>The reader checks fit, pricing concerns, Japanese usability, cancellation risk, and alternatives.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">3. Trial</p>
        <h2>Official page referral</h2>
        <p>When appropriate, the site sends readers to the official product page with clear disclosure.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
    <p>We check official pricing pages, help documents, terms, program notes, and real setup experience whenever possible. If a product has not been fully tested yet, we separate research notes from hands-on experience. Pricing and terms can change, so readers are always encouraged to confirm final details on official pages.</p>
    <p>Related Japanese policy pages are available here: <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>, <a href="/review-policy/">Review Criteria</a>, and <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.</p>

    <h2>Partnership Fit</h2>
    <p>The site is a good fit for SaaS, AI, website-building, CRM, newsletter, ecommerce, analytics, and creator-tool programs that want Japanese educational content. It is especially suitable for products with free plans, trials, clear pricing, and practical small-business use cases.</p>
    <p>Products with unclear cancellation flows, aggressive billing, or limited relevance to solo operators may still be covered, but they will be framed cautiously. The editorial voice is deliberately practical, and occasionally a little humorous, because readers make better decisions when the explanation feels human.</p>

    <h2>Operator</h2>
    <p>TATSU operates Hitori Jigyo Lab as Founder / Publisher. He is based in Fukuoka, Japan, and has long-term experience as a self-employed operator. The site reflects a practical, implementation-focused viewpoint rather than a purely theoretical software review approach.</p>

